      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/c4cdca/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-04-29T10:50:25.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The best option is to use the unselected heroes as a \"sidekick deck\", where you have access to a different incapacitated power each turn. See here:</p><p>http://www.boardgamegeek.com/thread/872326/my-journey-to-find-the-best-rules-for-a-2-players</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Otherwise, playing a 3 hero game while running 2 of the complexity 1 heroes (Legacy + Wraith together aren't nearly as complicated as Absolute Zero is alone) can be a viable alternative, even for new players.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:28:53.381Z",
